From 7797aeaaccb58759b67324d802f44059085d3f5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sardi-dev <134648583+sardi-dev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:33:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/25] Apply module SQL files in the database updater

Modules had no way to ship database content: their scripts are registered
after the world data is loaded, so a module could not add its own tables or
rows in time.

The updater now also reads modules/<module>/data/sql/db-auth, db-characters
and db-world after the core updates of the same database. Files run once, in
module name order and then file name order, and are recorded in
skyfire_db_updates as <module>/<file>, so an edited file is handled like an
edited core update. A failing file stops startup like a failing core update.
The baseline mode does not record module files as applied.

Updates.Modules turns it off, Updates.ModulesSqlPath overrides the folder
(default: the modules folder next to SqlPath). The module SQL is installed to
<prefix>/modules/<module>/data/sql. The folder layout is the one AzerothCore
uses for module SQL.
